     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Hi all,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Tomorrow I will give a talk on using <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">lapply</code> to automate, using <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">apply</code> to do things that are easy in Excel but can seem hard in R, and writing your own functions. The idea is that a few key functions and idioms unlock a lot of power, but many researchers never come across them and so struggle with data manipulation and copy-and-paste code to do repetitive computations. It should be pretty beginner-friendly, and I am happy for it to be interactive, so if you have been struggling with something like this or have questions that fit the topic, bring them. As always, we will livecast (<a href=\"https://plus.google.com/events/cchhif4q8q00k7u495me3i4v6q0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://plus.google.com/events/cchhif4q8q00k7u495me3i4v6q0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467334828000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2eReU_03DLsikpTNTHd-mP\">link</a>), and make the video available afterward. Here is the blurb:</p>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;border-left-width:4px;border-left-style:solid;border-left-color:rgb(221,221,221);padding:0px 1em;color:rgb(119,119,119);quotes:none\">\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">​Access the power of R through the apply-family of functions and by writing your own functions. You’ll save time, headaches, and mistakes. This is an “advanced-beginner” talk intended to get people started or more comfortable with automation. If you find yourself copy-and-pasting R code, this is for you! If you have multiple data files to process, this is for you! If you want to become an R wizard but aren’t sure what the next steps are, this is for you!</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">The talk is Monday at 1:10 in Wickson 1017. ​After the talk, we’ll have the usual work session until 3:00.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">See you tomorrow,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Michael Levy</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">PhD Candidate<br>Department of Environmental Science and Policy<br>University of California, Davis<br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mal...@ucdavis.edu</a><br><a href=\"http://www.michaellevy.name/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.michaellevy.name/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467334828000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3OgJ9KbcS2ivEi61advqF2\">www.michaellevy.name</a></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdiBjbGFzcz0iZ21haWxfZGVmYXVsdCIgc3R5bGU9ImZvbnQtZmFtaWx5OiB0YWhvbWEsIHNh\r\nbnMtc2VyaWY7IGZvbnQtc2l6ZTogc21hbGw7Ij5IaSBhbGwsPC9kaXY+PGRpdiBjbGFzcz0iZ21h\r\naWxfZGVmYXVsdCIgc3R5bGU9ImZvbnQtZmFtaWx5OiB0YWhvbWEsIHNhbnMtc2VyaWY7IGZvbnQt\r\nc2l6ZTogc21hbGw7Ij48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdiBjbGFzcz0iZ21haWxfZGVmYXVsdCIgc3R5bGU9\r\nImZvbnQtZmFtaWx5OiB0YWhvbWEsIHNhbnMtc2VyaWY7IGZvbnQtc2l6ZTogc21hbGw7Ij5Ub21v\r\ncnJvdyBJIHdpbGwgZ2l2ZSBhIHRhbGsgb24gdXNpbmcgYGxhcHBseWAgdG8gYXV0b21hdGUsIHVz\r\naW5nIGBhcHBseWAgdG8gZG8gdGhpbmdzIHRoYXQgYXJlIGVhc3kgaW4gRXhjZWwgYnV0IGNhbiBz\r\nZWVtIGhhcmQgaW4gUiwgYW5kIHdyaXRpbmcgeW91ciBvd24gZnVuY3Rpb25zLiBUaGUgaWRlYSBp\r\ncyB0aGF0IGEgZmV3IGtleSBmdW5jdGlvbnMgYW5kIGlkaW9tcyB1bmxvY2sgYSBsb3Qgb2YgcG93\r\nZXIsIGJ1dCBtYW55IHJlc2VhcmNoZXJzIG5ldmVyIGNvbWUgYWNyb3NzIHRoZW0gYW5kIHNvIHN0\r\ncnVnZ2xlIHdpdGggZGF0YSBtYW5pcHVsYXRpb24gYW5kIGNvcHktYW5kLXBhc3RlIGNvZGUgdG8g\r\nZG8gcmVwZXRpdGl2ZSBjb21wdXRhdGlvbnMuIE